KNOWNBUG: N5008 [class.base.init]/6 + [temp.variadic]/5 -- std::pair's
out-of-line DELEGATING piecewise constructor.  The delegation target is a
member constructor template with FOUR zipped packs (two type packs, two
non-type index packs); resolving it inside the mem-initializer fails, the
swallowed error leaves the piecewise instance with an empty body, and the
constructed pair keeps garbage.  This is the remaining front-end blocker
of cpp20_map_basic (first insert stores a garbage key; unbounded
unwinding then diverges on the nondet-shaped tree).  Bisection: delegation
to a non-pack target works (d7), direct calls of the four-pack ctor work
(d11), delegation to a four-pack target fails (single resolve throw in
typecheck_member_initializer).  g++/clang++ runtime-verified.  Flip to
CORE when the mixed four-pack deduction resolves in the mem-initializer
context.
